    "chunk_size_bytes": 1251,
    "chunk_text": "Family politics is now over in Sri Lanka - President\n\nColombo, Sep. 13 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake today said that the era of political dynasties is over, saying the practice of a President\u2019s son succeeding him or a Prime Minister\u2019s son inheriting the premiership belongs to Sri Lanka\u2019s \u201cold politics\u201d and is not part of modern politics.\n\nAddressing a public gathering at the Sinharagama Grounds in Nochchiyagama today, the President said the people had made a clear decision to move away from the traditional political culture at the September 21, 2024 election.\n\n\u201cIn our country, people generally used to think that if the father is the President, the son must also become the President. If the father is the Prime Minister, the son must also become the Prime Minister. That politics belongs to an old era\u2014that is not modern politics,\u201d he said.\n\nPresident Dissanayake said the 2024 election represented a decision by the people to change that political culture.\n\nHe said the government was focused on creating a new political culture rather than continuing practices associated with the country\u2019s previous political system.\n\nThe President also said there were no political threats facing his administration."
  },
