    "chunk_size_bytes": 666,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan long-haul jet owner arrives at Ratmalana\n\nColombo, Sep. 13 (Daily Mirror) - Dr. Rosh Jalagge, the first Sri Lankan to own a private long-haul jet, arrived at the Ratmalana Airport in his private aircraft, according to airport sources.\n\nDr. Jalagge arrived in Sri Lanka aboard his private jet, marking a notable development in the country\u2019s private aviation sector.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s first privately owned aircraft was a Learjet 35A purchased by businessman Upali Wijewardene in the 1980s.\n\nThe arrival of Dr. Jalagge\u2019s long-haul jet highlights the significant changes in Sri Lanka\u2019s private aviation landscape since the introduction of the Learjet 35A."
