    "chunk_text": "Hilton Colombo celebrates 39 years at heart of  Sri Lankan hospitality\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s flagship Hilton property reflects on nearly four decades of iconic occasions, culinary experiences and warm hospitality in heart of Colombo\n\nHilton Colombo marks its 39th anniversary this September, celebrating nearly four decades as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s pioneering international hotels and the flagship Hilton property in the country.\n\nSince opening in 1987, the hotel has grown alongside Colombo itself, becoming a familiar part of the city\u2019s story and a place where international travellers, local guests, world leaders, families and generations of team members have come together.\n\nOver the years, Hilton Colombo has been the setting for moments that have shaped both the hotel and the city around it. The hotel has hosted Commonwealth Heads of State, former US presidents and visiting dignitaries, while its event spaces have hosted occasions ranging from CHOGM 2013 and Colombo Fashion Week to official state banquets and national celebrations.\n\nMore than 20,000 weddings have been celebrated at the hotel, making Hilton Colombo part of countless family stories spanning across generations.\n\nThe hotel\u2019s role in Colombo has extended well beyond accommodation. With 368 guestrooms and suites, six restaurants and bars and 2,891 square metres of meetings and events space, Hilton Colombo has long served as a meeting point for business, celebration and leisure.\n\nIts pillar-less Grand Ballroom has welcomed some of the city\u2019s most significant corporate and social gatherings, while venues such as The Blue and Ruby have provided distinctive settings for occasions both large and intimate.\n\nHilton Colombo has also played a defining role in the city\u2019s dining and social landscape. Graze Kitchen presents international and local cuisine through its signature show kitchens, whilst Emperor\u2019s Wok, the hotel\u2019s specialty Chinese restaurant, showcases the fine-dining heritage of the Chinese cuisine."
