    "md5": "e618f28e9ff900a634f914953f881c0f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1993,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Thailand sign landmark agreements to strengthen labour cooperation\n\nSri Lanka and Thailand today signed two landmark agreements aimed at strengthening labour cooperation and creating structured employment opportunities for Sri Lankan workers in Thailand.\n\nThe Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Labour Cooperation and the Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) on the Employment of Sri Lankan Workers in Thailand were signed by Sri Lankan Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and Thai Labour Minister Julapun Amornvivat.\n\nThe agreements establish a transparent and structured framework for the recruitment and employment of Sri Lankan workers while ensuring their rights, welfare and protection.\n\nThe Thai Cabinet has approved the recruitment of an initial 10,000 Sri Lankan workers under the new legal framework to help address labour shortages in Thailand.\n\nThe MoU provides for cooperation in areas including labour policies and practices, labour market information, skills development, labour productivity and labour protection, as well as measures to prevent illegal recruitment and human trafficking.\n\nThe MoA sets out practical arrangements covering recruitment procedures, employment contracts, legal protection, welfare, visas and work permits, and return and repatriation of workers.\n\nMinister Herath welcomed the opportunity for Sri Lankan workers to seek employment in Thailand and stressed the importance of protecting their rights, welfare and social security.\n\nHe also called for the establishment of a Joint Working Group to monitor and review the implementation of the agreements. He further requested Thailand to consider expanding employment opportunities for Sri Lankan youth, particularly in the information technology and tourism sectors.\n\nMinister Julapun said Sri Lankan workers recruited under the framework would enjoy equal rights and protection under Thai labour law, including legally mandated wages, benefits and healthcare."
