    "chunk_size_bytes": 1945,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cA book is a beginning, but a habit is what changes a life. This year we are moving from giving books to building readers, week after week, in the schools that need it most. Reading should never be a privilege,\u201d Ragulan said.\n\nThe summit reflected the movement\u2019s increasingly broad reach, bringing together business leaders, authors, educators and literary figures.\n\nRagulan\u2019s second novel, \u2018The Last Cup of Tea\u2019, was also launched at the summit, bringing a deeply personal dimension to an event focused on the value of reading.\n\nThe book explores motherhood, identity, loss and transformation, built around Ragulan\u2019s idea that a woman is, in a sense, born twice - first as a woman and again when she becomes a mother.\n\nHe reflected on how families celebrate the birth of a child while rarely recognising that the same moment also marks the birth of a mother.\n\nThe final section of the book moves into fiction, with its family, characters and story shaped by personal experiences and emotions.\n\n\u201cThe feeling behind it is not,\u201d he said, explaining that although the story is fictional, some of the moments and emotions behind it came from experiences through which he had come to understand himself.\n\nThe book, he said, is not only about his own mother but about motherhood in a wider human context.\n\nAlongside Pathirana, John Keells Group OCTAVE Chief Growth Officer\u00a0 Rohan Jayaweera spoke on \u2018Readers\u2019 Advantage: Winning in the Age of AI\u2019, while leadership educator Vidusha Nathavitharana spoke on the value of reading from his childhood and revealed the \u2018Books that he would save from a fire\u2019.\n\nModerated by corporate trainer Prassanna Pathmanathan, a panel featuring Gratiaen Prize-winning writer Dr. Ramya Jirasinghe, award-winning author and administrative officer Ciara Mandulee, and Sarasavi Bookshop Director Amendra Haputhanthri discussed how a simple thought can develop until it becomes a novel or a book."
  },
