    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5f13b07244d43e97189d4e453a4b4a81",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1619,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Solar commissions 3MW Veyangoda Ground-Mounted Solar Project\n\nA commemorative plaque being presented to Ports and Civil Aviation Minister and Energy Minister Anura Karunathilake (right) by Managing Director Hasith Premathillake (centre) and Hayleys Fentons Deputy Managing Director \u2013 Energy Roshane Perera\n\nHayleys Solar marked a major milestone in its renewable energy journey with the opening of its 3MW Veyangoda Ground-Mounted Solar Project, with Energy Minister Anura Karunathilake gracing the occasion.\n\nThe project marks the first of Hayleys Solar\u2019s planned 300MW portfolio of ground-mounted solar power projects across Sri Lanka, further strengthening its commitment to expanding large-scale renewable energy solutions.\n\nHayleys Solar is part of Hayleys Fentons Ltd., under the Hayleys Group \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s most diversified blue-chip conglomerate with a business legacy spanning nearly 150 years across 17 sectors. The Veyangoda project reflects the Group\u2019s continued investment in expanding its renewable energy footprint in line with its long-standing commitment to sustainable innovation and nation-building.\n\nLocated adjacent to the Aththanagalla Oya, the project was designed to withstand challenging environmental conditions, including potential flooding during heavy rainfall. Following a detailed assessment using historical data from the Irrigation Department, Hayleys Solar implemented an elevated solar mounting structure with increased clearance and safety margins, together with elevated inverter supports and customised cable routing systems to enhance the project\u2019s resilience."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
