    "chunk_id": "2026-09-15-dailymirrorlk-e5f67922-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "16a5f3c76e3a665e786a6e19f0e9f8b9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1997,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan Corporate Health & Productivity Awards 2026 launched\n\nThe Sri Lankan Corporate Health & Productivity Awards (SLCHPA) 2026 was officially launched recently, introducing an enhanced edition of the platform that recognises organisations committed to strengthening employee wellbeing, workplace health and productivity across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe launch marks the beginning of a new chapter for an initiative that continues to encourage businesses to place their people at the centre of organisational success.\n\nOrganised by the Chamber of Lankan Entrepreneurs (COYLE), in partnership with the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO), and powered by Sampath Bank PLC as the Title Partner, SLCHPA 2026 aims to celebrate organizations that recognise the importance of investing in their people as a foundation for sustainable business growth. Through this partnership, JETRO brings Japanese expertise and global perspectives on workplace wellbeing and productivity, further strengthening the Awards\u2019 focus on promoting internationally relevant workplace practices across Sri Lanka.\n\nSince its inception, SLCHPA has evolved into a platform that encourages businesses to look beyond traditional measures of success and recognise the role of a healthy, engaged workforce in driving organisational performance. Over the years, the Awards have highlighted organisations that have introduced impactful workplace initiatives while inspiring companies across sectors to continuously improve their approach towards employee wellbeing, workplace culture and productivity.\n\nBuilding on this strong foundation, SLCHPA 2026 will be bigger and better, with a renewed focus on recognising more organisations, showcasing innovative workplace initiatives and creating greater value for participating companies. The Awards will provide businesses with an opportunity to benchmark their practices, gain national recognition and demonstrate their commitment towards creating workplaces where employees can thrive."
  },
