    "chunk_text": "With Sri Lanka\u2019s consumer base limited to just 22 million people, smaller than metropolitan Mumbai, Dr. Perera urged the retailers to tap regional integration, leverage the bilateral free trade agreements and plug into the regional value chains, pointing to India\u2019s over 400-million-strong middle class as an accessible supply and consumer base.\n\nDrawing parallels to the emerging market success stories such as the Philippines\u2019 Jollibee, Brazil\u2019s Havaianas, South Korea\u2019s beauty sector and Sri Lanka\u2019s own Dilmah, Dwibedi asserted that the local brands do not need to dilute their native identity to succeed overseas.\n\n\u201cBuild an international brand but you don\u2019t need to look international,\u201d Dwibedi said, emphasising that the authentic domestic heritage and storytelling resonate globally when paired with the local customisation and hero products.\n\nAddressing the capital constraints within the domestic financial system, Dwibedi urged the retailers to leverage their domestic proof-of-concept to attract foreign direct investment (FDI) and private equity to scale the regional operations.\n\n\u201cIf you\u2019re worried about capital, you can tap outside international capital. You can tap international capital through partnerships, joint ventures or strategic M&A,\u201d Dwibedi noted.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s almost like you\u2019re going to a country, telling that private equity: \u2018I am from Sri Lanka. I have done this. I have this product proposition. I took it to the market. I want the money to expand.\u2019 The difference is that you have a proven track record in Sri Lanka.\u201d\n\nDwibedi also pointed to Sri Lanka\u2019s reviving tourism sector as an underutilised springboard for global brand trial and digital customer acquisition. Recounting his personal habit of purchasing local herbal wellness remedies, such as the herbal tea sachets for sore throats, during visits to the island, he highlighted how the tourist footfall can initiate a broader international discovery cycle."
