    "md5": "ae8fb737f7336bcf1ac632b3bdea1b87",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1934,
    "chunk_text": "On the IMF, the summit reaffirmed the need for a strong, quota-based and adequately resourced IMF at the centre of the global financial safety net to effectively support its members, particularly the most vulnerable countries.\n\nIt also reaffirmed that the 2025 World Bank Shareholding Review is a critical tool to strengthen multilateralism and enhance the legitimacy of the World Bank Group.\n\nThe summit noted that the multilateral trading system has long been at a crossroads. The proliferation of trade-restrictive actions inconsistent with WTO rules\u2014whether indiscriminate rising of tariffs and non-tariff measures or protectionism under the guise of environmental objectives \u2014 threatens to further reduce global trade, disrupt supply chains and introduce uncertainty, potentially exacerbating economic disparities.\n\nThe DD voiced serious concerns about the rise of unilateral tariff and non-tariff measures which distort trade and are inconsistent with WTO rules. The Summit pledged to work together to enhance the WTO\u2019s responsiveness to the needs of emerging markets and developing economies.\n\nThe summit underscored that security among all countries is indivisible and reiterated BRICS\u2019 commitment to the peaceful resolution of international disputes through dialogue, consultation and diplomacy. It encouraged the active role of regional organisations in conflict prevention and resolution,\u00a0 and highlighted the importance of preventive diplomacy and mediation, with the consent of relevant parties.\n\nThe summit expressed deep concern over the continued escalation of tensions in the Middle East/West Asia without naming specific countries or non-state actors. It called for maximum restraint and avoidance of actions that could further aggravate the situation, urging protection of civilians and civilian infrastructure in accordance with the UN Charter, including respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity."
