    "chunk_size_bytes": 1846,
    "chunk_text": "The summit expressed deep concern over the continued escalation of tensions in the Middle East/West Asia without naming specific countries or non-state actors. It called for maximum restraint and avoidance of actions that could further aggravate the situation, urging protection of civilians and civilian infrastructure in accordance with the UN Charter, including respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity.\n\nOn Gaza, it called for the implementation of relevant UNGA and UNSC resolutions and urged all parties to ensure maintenance of the ceasefire and full, unhindered humanitarian access. It expressed deep concern over continued violence in Gaza despite the October 2025 ceasefire agreement.\n\nIt reaffirmed that a just and lasting solution to the Israeli-Palestinian conflict can only be achieved by peaceful means and depends on fulfilment of the legitimate rights of the Palestinian people, including self-determination and return.\n\nIt affirmed the need for adequate representation of Palestine in relevant international organisations and reaffirmed support for the State of Palestine\u2019s full membership in the UN as a sovereign, independent and viable State of Palestine within the 1967 borders, including the Gaza Strip and the West Bank, with East Jerusalem as its capital.\n\nThough the DD used strong words on the West Asian crisis, it chose not to name Israel and the US as aggressors in order not to alienate them from the proposed negotiations. The other consideration was that host India has close relations with the US and Israel.\n\nOn terrorism, the summit expressed strong condemnation of any acts of terrorism as criminal and unjustifiable, regardless of motivation. \u201cWe condemn in the strongest terms the terrorist attack in Jammu and Kashmir on 22 April 2025, during which 26 people were killed and many more injured."
