    "chunk_text": "In an exclusive interview with the Daily Mirror, General Silva spoke about how the final humanitarian operation unfolded, false narratives created by LTTE sympathizers living overseas, pain endured by civilians affected by the conflict and challenges faced during COVID-19 pandemic recovery efforts.\n\nQYou have had an illustrious career in the Army spanning 40 years. How does it feel like to retire from active service?\n\nQ Could you explain how the final humanitarian operation unfolded ?\n\nIt\u2019s important to understand the nature of the threat that the country and armed forces faced at that particular time. The LTTE was internationally regarded as one of the most ruthless terrorist organizations. They carried out over thousands of suicide attacks across the country. They were the pioneers of modern suicide terrorism. They assassinated many political leaders in Sri Lanka as well as overseas from Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi to President Ranasinghe Premadasa and injured Mrs. Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga; who was injured following an attack. They also forcibly recruited child soldiers. They were doing ethnic cleansing and repeatedly attacked civilians. This is what the LTTE did prior to the commencement of the humanitarian operation in 2006."
