    "chunk_text": "It\u2019s important to understand the nature of the threat that the country and armed forces faced at that particular time. The LTTE was internationally regarded as one of the most ruthless terrorist organizations. They carried out over thousands of suicide attacks across the country. They were the pioneers of modern suicide terrorism. They assassinated many political leaders in Sri Lanka as well as overseas from Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi to President Ranasinghe Premadasa and injured Mrs. Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga; who was injured following an attack. They also forcibly recruited child soldiers. They were doing ethnic cleansing and repeatedly attacked civilians. This is what the LTTE did prior to the commencement of the humanitarian operation in 2006.\n\nThis operation wasn\u2019t against civilians. The government\u2019s responsibility and the task that we were assigned to do was to rescue civilians and to liberate the land from the clutches of the LTTE. We accomplished our task by rescuing civilians from LTTE-dominated areas, by liberating the land and achieving peace. Unfortunately the terrorist sympathizers are not happy.\n\nQThere are numerous attempts by LTTE sympathizers and propagandists who highlight atrocities committed by armed forces during the final stages of the war. What do you have to say about these narratives?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
