    "chunk_text": "Dr. Nanayakkara claimed that funds allocated for sterilisation had not been fully utilised, with around Rs. 100 million of the Rs. 200 million allocated in 2024 being spent, while only about Rs. 48 million had been utilised from the 2025 allocation.\n\nHe said arrangements were also being finalised for the Government and private sector to provide free rabies vaccination and sterilisation services for both stray and owned dogs.\n\nUnder the new system, samples could be obtained from the neck area, while rabies testing facilities would be expanded to 25 centres across the country.\n\nDr. Nanayakkara urged the public to read the actual legislation rather than relying on sensational claims circulating on social media.\n\n\u201cThere is no provision for a \u2018dog tax\u2019, nor does feeding an animal automatically make a person its legal owner,\u201d he said."
