    "chunk_id": "2026-09-16-dailymirrorlk-9c083322-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e2dfc54ecb785262a43d487201a6d7df",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "SLASSCOM to lead delegation to Kenya this month\n\nSLASSCOM will lead its GT&I Market Access \u2013 Africa Delegation to Nairobi, Kenya, on 25 September, creating opportunities for Sri Lankan technology companies to connect with potential clients, partners and key business organisations in Kenya and explore pathways into the wider East African market.\n\nOrganised in collaboration with the Sri Lankan High Commission in Kenya, the delegation aims to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2013Kenya business and technology ties through direct market engagement and strategic business meetings.\n\nSix SLASSCOM member companies will participate in the delegation: NCINGA, Gift O, hSenidBiz, MillenniumIT ESP, Sterling BPO Solutions (Pvt) Ltd and Global Frontiers.\n\nAs part of the programme, participating companies will have the opportunity to engage with William Kabogo Gitau, Cabinet Secretary, Ministry of Information, Communications and the Digital Economy, Kenya, as well as key Kenyan organisations and potential business partners, including the Kenya Investment Authority, Kenya National Chamber of Commerce and Industry (KNCCI), LASER Infrastructure & Technology Solutions (LITES) Ltd, and Technology Service Providers of Kenya.\n\nSampath Jayasundara, Chairperson, SLASSCOM said, \u201cAfrica presents an important growth opportunity for Sri Lanka\u2019s knowledge and innovation industry, with Kenya offering a strong gateway into the wider region. This delegation is about moving beyond market exploration and creating the right connections for Sri Lankan companies to build real commercial partnerships.\u201d\n\nRuvini De Silva, Acting High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to Kenya said, \u201cKenya continues to experience significant economic and digital development. Initiatives such as this delegation can play an important role in connecting businesses, building confidence and creating new avenues for collaboration between our countries.\u201d"
  },
