    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Thailand move to expedite visa-free travel for ordinary passport holders\n\nColombo, Sep. 16 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka and Thailand have agreed to further strengthen bilateral relations, with discussions focusing on expediting arrangements for a visa exemption for ordinary passport holders.\n\nThe agreement was reached during a meeting between Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and Thailand\u2019s Acting Foreign Minister Sarun Charoensuwan in Bangkok.\n\nThe proposed visa exemption is expected to facilitate travel and tourism while promoting greater people-to-people exchanges between the two countries.\n\nDuring the meeting, the two sides also discussed expanding cooperation in trade, investment, tourism, labour mobility, education, maritime security and cultural exchanges.\n\nBoth sides reaffirmed their commitment to deepening Sri Lanka-Thailand relations and advancing practical areas of cooperation for the mutual benefit of the people of both countries."
  },
