    "chunk_text": "More than the numbers \u2014 how Sri Lanka\u2019s finance professionals can become trusted strategic advisers\n\nAs Sri Lanka continues its economic recovery and reform journey, businesses and policymakers need more than an accurate account of the past. They need finance professionals who can anticipate change, assess risk, identify opportunities and connect financial insight to long-term strategy\n\nOver the past few decades, the profession has evolved beyond a pure compliance remit as we, finance and accounting professionals, have established ourselves as effective business partners. While we still ensure that our organisations meet their legal obligations, we also help to drive business growth, enhance operational efficiency, fund innovation, manage risk and inform leadership decision-making. Undoubtedly, accounting and finance professionals have played a pivotal role in our organisations\u2019 success to date.\n\nAlthough we have achieved much, we should not be complacent, however. The fast-moving nature of today\u2019s business environment demands that we keep evolving and reinventing ourselves. In fact, I believe we are on the cusp of an exciting inflection point. We are about to make the leap from business partner to strategic adviser, enabled by new technological tools and our enhanced human capabilities.\n\nAs strategic advisers, we will create new value by providing the indispensable insights and knowledge that will enable our organisations to seize new market opportunities, pre-solve major problems and flourish in a world that will be defined by the transition to a more sustainable economy and advances in artificial intelligence (AI). So how can we evolve from where we are now to being the trusted strategic advisers of the future?"
  },
