    "chunk_text": "Gold mine collapse kills at least 70 people in Sudan\u2019s West Kordofan\n\nAl Jazeera -\u00a0At least 70 people have been killed after a gold mine collapsed in Sudan\u2019s West Kordofan state.\n\nDozens of artisanal miners were killed and a number of them were trapped after a series of adjoining mining shafts collapsed at al-Zaraa mine, near al-Nuhud town, on Tuesday, the Kordofan Observatory monitoring group said on Wednesday.\n\nThe group added that no specialised rescue teams had joined the rescue effort and residents with rudimentary tools were struggling to pull survivors out in loose and sandy soil.\n\nA source in the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF), which controls the area, told the AFP news agency that at least 82 people were killed and another 50 wounded. \u201cThere is an unknown number of people still trapped under the rubble and rescue efforts are being conducted with rudimentary methods,\u201d the source, who requested anonymity because he was not authorised to speak to the media, said.\n\nKhair al-Sayyed Jabara, who survived the incident, told AFP on Wednesday that he and fellow miners had dug throughout the night using their tools to reach survivors, adding that heavy equipment was needed.\n\nAnother miner, Amin Suleiman, said the shafts were packed so closely that each one pulled down those beside it when it collapsed.\n\nLocal sources told the Reuters news agency that the high death toll was due to \u2060a lack of safety procedures and rescue equipment.\n\nSudan Doctors Network, a Khartoum-based medical group, said search efforts were ongoing and the casualty figure could rise, adding that the site was missing basic safeguards for workers.\n\nThe group condemned the \u201cnegligence\u201d it said put miners\u2019 lives at serious risk.\n\nWest Kordofan is held by the paramilitary RSF, which has been fighting Sudan\u2019s army since April 2023. Smuggled gold has been a key source of revenue for the group."
