    "chunk_size_bytes": 2035,
    "chunk_text": "Anuradhapura shift: Beginning ends, end begins\n\nThe SLPP\u2019s Anuradhapura rally is occasion for my conclusion that the arc of the AKD Presidency and JVP-NPP rule has begun its parabolic descent. This does not mean a linear trajectory from Anuradhapura 2026 to the President\u2019s House 2029 for Namal Rajapaksa\u2014a scenario which is possible, but far from preordained\n\nMy caption this week is an obvious echo of Winston Churchill\u2019s characterisation at a nodal point in WWII, that it was not yet \u2018the beginning of the end\u2019, but only \u2018the end of the beginning\u2019. Later in the war, he announced the beginning of the end.\n\nThere is usually an interregnum between the two, but sometimes the transition is short, and at others, the end of the beginning marks the beginning of the end.\n\n\u2018Why Prabhakaran Will Lose\u2019 was the title of an article by me (then in my late-40s) which appeared prominently in the pages of The Sunday Island, Colombo, dated October 17th 2004. At a time when the political, academic and civic intelligentsia was wedded to the thesis of an \u2018unwinnable war\u2019, the title risked damage to my intellectual reputation and credibility by going beyond an assertion of \u2018Why Prabhakaran Won\u2019t Win\u2019\u2014which would mean a hurting stalemate\u2014to a definitive \u2018will lose\u2019. My unambiguous prediction was made the year before Mahinda Rajapaksa secured his party\u2019s Presidential candidacy, won the Presidency, and appointed Gotabaya Rajapaksa and Sarath Fonseka as Secretary/Defence and Army chief respectively. None of these were safely predictable.\n\nThough occasioned by Karuna\u2019s rebellion and the intra-LTTE mini civil war in the East, with Karuna already on the backfoot, my prognosis was grounded far more in the comparative study of successful asymmetric wars; Prabhakaran\u2019s sustained transgression of their characteristic features and norms; and the axiom of Vietnam\u2019s General Giap that \u201cif you override the objective laws of development of a phenomenon, those objective laws will override you\u201d."
  },
