    "chunk_size_bytes": 1868,
    "chunk_text": "Anuradhapura was a more organic mass mobilisation. The SLPP rally was energised by a cocktail of strong emotions\u2014overweening affection and respect for Mahinda Rajapaksa, combative loyalty to the incarcerated Namal Rajapaksa, open declaration of a determination to ensure Namal\u2019s election as President in 2029, renewed collective hope at that prospect, defiant resistance to the ruling JVP-NPP and reawakened bitter memories of JVP barbarism in the locality. (Especially poignant was the recollection of the JVP\u2019s murder in 1987 in the Anuradhapura bazaar, of Nandana Marasinghe, a hero of the JVP\u2019s April 1971 uprising). The mood was more upbeat and applause from the audience was far more spontaneous, animated, enthusiastic and frequent at SLPP/Anuradhapura.\n\nIt is not that the Anuradhapura discourse didn\u2019t have a downside. There was an occasional infusion of ultranationalism\u2014though not (yet) open chauvinism or racism\u2014coming more from the SLPP\u2019s old allies rather than the SLPP itself.\u00a0 It was also a pity\u2014or sadly symbolic\u2014that the scheduled closing speech by the SLPP\u2019s DV Chanaka got \u2018timed out\u2019 or was somehow \u2018crowded out\u2019.\n\nAKD\u2019s Polonnaruwa and Anuradhapura speeches had nothing of the appeal his oratory had in 2024. The thrill was gone. All he had was a surly negativism, a truculently articulated commitment to \u2018lawfare\u2019 (amounting to a McCarthyite witch-hunt) against the Rajapaksa family. No credible, constructive hope for an improved life was communicated. His appeal has been funnelled-down to reassuring and remotivating the JVP-NPP hardcore. The combative cockiness of AKD and other JVP-NPP leaders, is hollow.\n\nAKD has embarked on a highly polarising two-pronged project. The dynamic of polarisation that cannot possibly work in his favour; it can only undermine him and his Government, shrinking its space."
